* **`updateReadModeContents` (Lines 151-158 in `AppDataManager.js`)** : This part of the code is within the `AppDataManager` class, which handles synchronization of data between the UI (your tabs) and the underlying data storage.  This is *very* important for ensuring that changes are reflected correctly.
```javascript
    async saveAllTabsToServer() {
          // ... other code ...

        // Update read mode content <<<
        for (let i = 1; i <= 100; i++) {
          const tabEl = document.getElementById(`readmode-content-tab${i}`);
          if (tabEl) {
            tabEl.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true })); // VERY IMPORTANT
          }
