```
 *   **`dispatchEvent(new Event('input'))`:** This line is *crucial*.  After saving changes, it simulates an `'input'` event on each `readmode-content` element.  This triggers any event listeners that are waiting for changes to the content (like the ones that call `formatContent`). It's the key to keeping the display consistent with the data. It's a way to say, "Hey, the content of this tab *might* have changed; re-check it and re-apply any formatting or logic that depends on the content."

* `addMessageToCurrentChat` in `AppDataManager.js` (lines 93-97). This function ensures that all messages will be pushed to the message object before saving to the server.
```js
  addMessageToCurrentChat(messageObj) {
    if (this.appData.chats[this.appData.currentChatName]) {
        this.appData.chats[this.appData.currentChatName].push(messageObj); // push to the front
    } else {
